Participation in an illegal street race shall include, but not be limited to:
(1) arriving at a location for the purpose of assisting with or being a spectator at the illegal street race;
(2) lining up on the side of a public street or highway for the purpose of being a spectator at an illegal street race;
(3) gathering on private property open to the general public without the consent of the owner, operator, or agent thereof for the purpose of assisting with or being a spectator in an illegal street race;
(4) impeding the free public use of a public street or highway by actions, words, or physical barriers for the purpose of assisting with or being a spectator in an illegal street race;
(5) lining up a motor vehicle alongside one or more additional motor vehicles for the purpose of assisting with an illegal street race;
(6) revving an engine or spinning a vehicle's tire in preparation for an illegal street race;
(7) being stationed at or near one or more motor vehicles serving as a race starter for an illegal street race;
(8) riding in an illegal street race vehicle as a passenger;
(9) assisting the organizers and/or drivers in carrying out an illegal street race; or
(10) exchanging money or anything of value with any driver, car owner, or other participant in connection with an illegal street race.
(Ord. No. 2021-004, § 1, 1-12-2021)

